        "Dieter Vollhardt"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Dynamical mean-field theory supplied a decisive and widely useful nonperturbative framework for correlated electrons.",
        "attribution": "Vollhardt and collaborators established the infinite-dimensional foundation, while Georges and Kotliar made the modern method and its physical reach decisive.",
        "maturity": "DMFT is a mature, extensively benchmarked framework with major influence on materials theory.",
